  "rationale": "Actual calibration inputs give a median slowest-state half-life of about 3 steps in the conditioning reverse scan, versus 59 in the forward scan. Double reverse state lifetimes by halving decay rates, and compensate each B-projection row to preserve its typical steady-state gain. For fixed delta, the exact compensation is (1-exp(-delta*A/2))/(1-exp(-delta*A)); each state uses the median ratio across channels with calibration-input mean deltas. This isolates longer temporal context from the gain increase of naive A scaling. No targets enter these factors; no derivatives or optimizer are used. Other recurrent blocks, delta parameters, C projections and skip D stay fixed.",
